ALX Garland's anihilation might be the  prettiest end of the world movie you'll  ever see based on the novel of the same  name by Jeff Vandermeer the movie tells  the story of a group of scientists  venturing into a strange quarantine zone  called the shimmer inside they encounter  a surreal world that seems to be remix  in itself and everything in it the film  juggles some heavy themes and has a lot  going on in its narrative so by the time  it ends it's a little difficult to  unpack let's break down the ending of  annihilation from a galaxy far away the  film's primary question is what is the  shimmer the film's opening shots show  some sort of interstellar object  careening through Earth's atmosphere and  crashing into a lighthouse which becomes  the prime destination for the research  and military expeditions into area X  which is what the land surrounding the  shimmer comes to be known as the shimmer  as it turns out is some sort of alien  force it's either a thinking living  breathing thing or a kind of celestial  cancer replicating itself unconsciously  either way its whole essence is  ultimately tied to an alien entity that  we see take on humanoid form in the  film's closing moments through the prism  annihilation second question is what  does the shimmer do determining this is  the primary goal of Lina's expedition  until her husband Cain came back nobody  who entered the shimmer ever returned  and he seems to be sick no longer fully  in control of himself and clearly in  pain with Kane out of commission the  area X crews still can't say for sure  what happens in the shimmer even after  throwing team after team into its  clutches until Lina and her crew journey  in despite the way our protagonists are  picked off one by one the shimmer isn't  an explicitly destructive force the land  inside is an a ravaged wasteland but a  lush exotic forest filled with surreal  flora and animals that only resemble  those native to earth the scientists  discovered that everything exposed to  the shimmer is in a constant accelerated  state of mutation and that mutation  isn't confined to singular DNA sets  instead the DNA is collectively jumbled  up animals become mixed with the plants  organic and inorganic materials combined  connecting all of nature in a very  literal very impossible way do you think  it's a crossroad we can't cross bridge  between different space  the end times it's established early on  in the film that the shimmer is  spreading as a scientist journey deeper  into its confines we see that Area X's  original headquarters has been  completely overtaken by the shimmer its  thread is made abundantly clear by  Jennifer Jason Leigh z-- dr. Ventress if  it goes unchecked the shimmer will  consume the world based on what we see  it'd be a gorgeous apocalypse but it's  still an apocalypse while beautiful the  shimmer is littered with corpses and  mutations and filled with an  overwhelming sense of dread humans in  the shimmer encounter violent ends like  Anya's death and the jaws of a mutant  bear or they give themselves over to it  in humans this DNA remix in leads to  madness making them disoriented agitated  and spaced out the film never makes a  statement on whether the shimmers  effects are a good or bad thing it  simply presents them as an inevitability  face to face toward the film's climax  Lina encounters dr. Ventress who has  finally made it to the lighthouse  however Ventress has become a part of  the alien force that created the shimmer  and she soon transcends her human form  and becomes a sort of fractal prism  herself after this prism absorbs a drop  of Lena's blood it takes on a humanoid  form in this moment Lena  effectively meets the shimmer while it  initially seems malicious the shimmer  never actually sets out to harm Lena  instead it just mirrors her movements  it's an important moment that embodies  the goals of the shimmer it seeks  understanding and integration it  assimilates to its environment the mass  mutations and prism effect are the  result smashing the mirror as their  confrontation with the shimmer creature  comes to a head the creature now in a  humanoid form and morphing into Lena is  given a grenade by the real Lena she  places it in the shimmers hands pulls  the pin and runs as the grenade explodes  the shimmer creature catches fire the  light house burns destroying the  entirety of the shimmer with it it  cements the idea that the shimmer is one  large collective beam and also allows  Lena the opportunity to escape and make  her way back to area X self-destruct  sequence  annihilation is a movie about  destruction the idea that deep in our  genetic coding there's a primal urge to  destroy ourselves in the world around us  the shimmer serves as an embodiment of  that inevitable urge it destroys what we  have and turns it into something new for  better or worse that penchant for  self-destruction is explored intensely  through our protagonists Lena is a woman  who ruins her marriage with an affair  indirectly influencing her husband to go  on what is potentially a one-way mission  Alma is a recovering addict Josie bears  the scars of self-harm Ventress is dying  of a cancer mutating their insides which  informs her fascination with the shimmer  these characters all have a subconscious  wish to end their lives so their  journeys ever deeper into the shimmer  have an air of inevitability  even though Lena survives she only does  so by destroying a doppelganger of  herself metaphorically wiping away her  old identity and emerging as something  new quarantine qat following her return  from the shimmer Lena is forced to take  part in an extensive debriefing about  her journey while under a strict  quarantine is it the real Lena or a  double after her time inside the shimmer  the truth is somewhere in between after  her questioning Lena is finally reunited  with Kaine who's no longer dying from  the shimmers effects and even seems  somewhat lucid what 